cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it."
type: dataset
title: "Gold Standard Carbon Project Registry (wss-carbon-registry)"
abstract: >-
  Point-in-time captures of the Gold Standard carbon project registry: every
  project's name, status, methodology, type, size, estimated annual credits and
  crediting period. The status vocabulary contains only three progression steps
  and no terminal state, so a project that loses certification has nowhere to be
  marked as having lost it. The public API has never been archived by the
  Internet Archive, and the registry's own web UI is a JavaScript application
  whose 68 archived captures are empty shells, so the register as it stood on a
  given date is not recoverable from anywhere else.
authors:
  - name: "q3dresearch"
    website: "https://github.com/q3dresearch"
# NO `license:` FIELD BY DEFAULT, ON PURPOSE. This template hard-coded
# CC-BY-4.0 until 2026-09-22, so every scaffolded repo claimed a grant nobody
# had checked. Add one only once you can name what the publisher grants, and
# write the reasoning into LICENSE-DATA. Absent means unspecified.
keywords:
  - git-scraping
  - open-data
  - point-in-time-data
  - dataset
